# Force LF in the working tree for everything text.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, the default from Git for
# Windows) rewrites the shell scripts to CRLF. bash then fails on the carriage
# returns with errors like:
#     $'\r': command not found
#     syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''
# which is confusing to diagnose because the file looks correct in an editor.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Be explicit for the executable scripts — these must never be CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

*.md  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
